 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the election law, in relation to authorizing computer\ngenerated registration lists; in relation to the list of supplies to be\ndelivered to poll sites",
    "basePrintNo": "S508",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S508-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd El L, generally",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S508\n\nSPONSOR: MYRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the election law, in relation to\nauthorizing computer generated registration lists; in relation to the\nlist of supplies to be delivered to poll sites\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo update the Election Law to recognize that many counties have the\ntechnology to employ computer generated registration lists at the poll\nsites, to make their use uniform, to update the list of supplies to be\ndelivered to the poll sites and to make certain gender neutral\ncorrections to the Election Law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThe bill amends Section 1-104 of the Election Law by adding a new\nsubsection (38) defining \"Computer generated registration list\" to be\nused in place of registration poll records to establish a person's\neligibility to vote in polling places on Election Day. The bill also\nsets forth the supplies to be provided to the polling sites for the new\nvoting systems. The bill replaces various masculine references in the\nElection Law with gender-neutral references. The bill also clarifies the\nlocation where certain information pertaining to voter information\nchanges and challenges is to be recorded on the computer generated\nregistration lists and the challenge report and the manner in which same\nshould be returned to the board of elections.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe advent of the new voting systems makes certain updates in the equip-\nment to be supplied to poll sites imperative. The computerization of\nregistration lists and their use at the poll sites is already authorized\nby Election Law 5-506(3)*. Guidance as to the use of computer-generated\nlists must be provided. The requirement that the computer generated\nregistration list be in printed form is 'outdated', and fails to consid-\ner or enable the many administrative and Election Day benefits the tech-\nnology offers.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2016 - S.6581: Committed to Rules./A.8608A:Passed.\n2017/2018 - S.2788: Referred to Senate Elections/A.5547: Passed the\nAssembly\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state and optional to the counties.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first of January nex.E.,Sueteding the\ndate on which it shall have become a law.\n",
